@page "/blazor-smoke"
@page "/admin/blazor-smoke"
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "RequireAdmin")]
@rendermode InteractiveServer

@*
    Temporary Phase 1 smoke-test page (plan §5 Phase 1, deliverable 7). Proves, end to end, that
    the Blazor hosting foundation, auth plumbing and per-page interactivity all actually work:
    - RequireAdmin authorization on a routable component (an unauthenticated request must
      redirect to /Account/Login, not 404/500).
    - An Interactive Server circuit opens and its counter button actually updates the DOM.
    - The second, nested route (/admin/blazor-smoke) guards a known .NET 10 regression where
      blazor.web.js resolved _blazor/initializers relative to a nested path instead of the app
      base, 404ing and leaving the circuit dead (see tests/DiscordBot.E2E). Both routes point at
      the same component deliberately, so the flat-route and nested-route Playwright checks run
      against one build.
    Deleted once the real probe page (/blazor-probe, plan §5 Phase 1 deliverable 7, landing in a
    later wave once the event bus / toast / theme interop / chart pieces exist) replaces it.
*@

<PageTitle>Blazor Smoke Test</PageTitle>

<h1>Blazor Smoke Test</h1>

<p role="status">Current count: @_count</p>
<button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="Increment">Click me</button>

@code {
    private int _count;

    private void Increment() => _count++;
}
